{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSZG8fUcNuNwutr1QWXB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add an `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class. Create an `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method that:\n   - Finds the order by ID (throws 404 if not found)\n   - If already CANCELLED, returns it without changes (idempotent)\n   - If ACTIVE, checks if any shipment is CONFIRMED (throws 409 if found)\n   - If check passes, updates order to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Returns the cancelled order\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add a method to find shipments by order ID so we can check and update shipments.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Modify the create endpoint to check if the order is CANCELLED and throw 409 if it is.\n\n5. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add a method `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` to return all shipments for an order.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for the case when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order), and potentially `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (when trying to cancel an order with CONFIRMED shipments).\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests for cancel functionality.\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for preventing shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered putting the cancel logic in a separate service class, but since the existing code is simple and doesn't have a service layer, I'll keep the logic in the controller to match the existing patterns.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (cancel ACTIVE order)**:\n   - POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller finds order by ID\n   - Order is ACTIVE\n   - Controller queries ShipmentRepository for all shipments with this orderId\n   - No CONFIRMED shipments found\n   - Controller updates order status to CANCELLED\n   - Controller updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Returns the cancelled order with 200 OK\n\n2. **Idempotent case (cancel already CANCELLED order)**:\n   - POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller finds order by ID\n   - Order is already CANCELLED\n   - Returns the order without changes with 200 OK\n\n3. **Error case (CONFIRMED shipment exists)**:\n   - POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller finds order by ID\n   - Order is ACTIVE\n   - Controller queries for shipments\n   - CONFIRMED shipment found\n   - Throws ConflictException with error code (needs new code)\n   - Returns 409 with error body, order and shipments unchanged\n\n4. **Error case (order not found)**:\n   - POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller tries to find order\n   - Not found\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException\n   - Returns 404 with error body\n\n5. **Error case (create shipment for CANCELLED order)**:\n   - POST `/shipments` with orderId of CANCELLED order\n   - ShipmentController checks if order exists and is CANCELLED\n   - Throws ConflictException\n   - Returns 409 with error body\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n- Test cancelling an ACTIVE order cancels CREATED shipments and returns 200\n- Test cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds without changes\n- Test cancelling with a CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409\n- Test cancelling a non-existent order fails with 404\n\nShipmentControllerTest additions:\n- Test creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order fails with 409\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_read_input_tokens":20580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1590},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d448a531-98c8-4868-8b2d-9ce3ac2ee4ef","uuid":"74c2ad2b-dc65-4b79-b677-0ca70831e2f1","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:53:28.944Z","request_id":"req_011CfSZG8ATyYPUD5j3UDowJ"}
