{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSZNdgQzpNxPMAVYNvSz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 22 tests passed including the 9 new tests I added. Let me verify the command and result:\n\n**Command**: `cd sample-service && ./mvnw test`\n\n**Result**: \n- Tests run: 22\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n- BUILD SUCCESS\n\nAll tests passed successfully, including:\n- 7 new tests in OrderControllerTest\n- 2 new tests in ShipmentControllerTest\n- All 4 existing OrderControllerTest tests still pass\n- All 5 existing ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass\n- All existing customer and application tests still pass\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** - `./mvnw test` completed with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** - All 13 existing tests still pass (4 OrderControllerTest + 5 ShipmentControllerTest + 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests + 3 CustomerControllerTest)\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order** - Implemented in OrderController.cancel() with test \"cancels an ACTIVE order and changes its status to CANCELLED\"\n   ✅ **Persists it** - Order is saved via repository.save()\n   ✅ **Cancels that order's CREATED shipments** - All CREATED shipments are found and updated to CANCELLED status with test \"cancelling an order cancels all CREATED shipments\"\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent** - Uses ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) following existing patterns\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds** - Test \"cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing\" verifies idempotency\n   ✅ **A cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing** - Test \"cancelling fails with 409 when order has CONFIRMED shipment\" and \"cancelling an order with both CREATED and CONFIRMED shipments fails\" verify all-or-nothing semantics\n   ✅ **An unknown order is refused** - Test \"cancelling returns 404 for non-existent order\" verifies ResourceNotFoundException\n   ✅ **A shipment for a cancelled order is refused** - Test \"rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order with 409\" verifies this\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** - No pom.xml modifications needed\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified core feature files\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added OrderStatus enum and status field with default ACTIVE. ✅ Necessary for tracking order state.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Added two new error codes: ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER. ✅ Necessary for API contract consistency.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added findByOrderId() method. ✅ Necessary to query shipments for an order during cancellation.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added orderRepository injection and check for cancelled orders when creating shipments. ✅ Necessary to enforce the business rule that shipments cannot be created for cancelled orders.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** - Added shipmentRepository injection and cancel() method that implements the cancellation logic. ✅ Necessary for the core functionality.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 7 new test methods and one reset change. ✅ Necessary to verify cancel functionality.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 2 new test methods and one reset change to include orderRepository. ✅ Necessary to test shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint allowing customers to cancel ACTIVE orders, making it idempotent, preventing cancellation when CONFIRMED shipments exist, and blocking shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum and status field (default ACTIVE)\n              ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER error codes\n  